The Latin subset's unicode-range (the same for all three, as Fontsource
declares it) is in site.css's @font-face rules. Characters outside it, such
as arrows and box-drawing marks, come from the system's fonts.

To check a file: shasum -a 256 <file>. To list a font's axes:
  uvx --from 'fonttools[woff]' python -c "from fontTools.ttLib import TTFont; \
    print([(a.axisTag, a.minValue, a.maxValue) for a in TTFont('<file>')['fvar'].axes])"
